<title>GERMANY: Daimler - can't confirm '96 profit statement.</title>
<headline>Daimler - can't confirm '96 profit statement.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokesman at Daimler-Benz AG would not officially confirm on Tuesday a 1996 profit figure provided to reporters by one of the industrial giant's board members at the Geneva motor show.</p>
<p>The spokesman said Daimler would not publish final results for 1996 until its scheduled annual news conference in April.</p>
<p>Daimler board member Eckhard Cordes had said on Monday night in Geneva that the company would post group net profits of at least two billion marks for 1996.</p>
<p>In 1995 the group posted a record 5.7 billion mark loss.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
